flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1{"Does the product meet quality assurance team product<br/>specifications?"}
    box_2["Identify and note the defect type on the non<br/>conforming part (e.g. a dent on the part surface)<br/>before proceeding."]
    box_3["Remove the non conforming parts and reload with a<br/>product batch that meets quality assurance team<br/>specifications."]
    box_4{"Is picking up part from supply conveyor correct?"}
    box_5["Complete the following checks: 1. Check by jogging<br/>whether the part pickup from the supply conveyor is<br/>correct and whether the part is correctly aligned<br/>under the vacuum head. 2. Check whether the assembly<br/>robot produces excessive retries during pickup."]
    box_6[/"Supply conveyor pickup diagnostic (GRAPH 09)"/]
    box_7{"Is part mounting correct?"}
    box_8["Verify that the part is mounted centred and straight<br/>from the indexing table, all actuators have reached<br/>their end positions, and all part lifters are at<br/>equal height."]
    box_9[/"Insert placement pickup diagnostic (GRAPH 08)"/]
    box_10[/"Part mounting adjustment procedure"/]
    box_11{"Is part control (vacuum) correct?"}
    box_12["Complete the following steps: 1. Refer to the vacuum<br/>part present detection diagnostic. 2. Check whether<br/>the correct vacuum pressure value is reached."]
    box_13[/"Refer to the vacuum pressure value check for variant<br/>B machines (medium format parts)."/]
    box_14[/"Refer to the vacuum pressure value check for variant<br/>C machines (large format parts)."/]
    box_15[/"Vacuum part present detection diagnostic"/]
    box_16{"Are there contaminated parts?"}
    box_17["Complete the following checks: 1. Check the assembly<br/>robot axis/axes for contamination. 2. Check the<br/>centering sleeve and vacuum tube for contamination."]
    box_18["Clean the contaminated assembly robot axis,<br/>centering sleeve, and vacuum tube."]
    box_19{"Are there electrical defects?"}
    box_20["Complete the following checks: 1. Check proximity<br/>sensor and cabling. 2. Check assembly robot for<br/>cable breaks. 3. Check the force sensor for<br/>electrical defects."]
    box_21["Replace the defective component identified in the<br/>inspection (proximity sensor, cabling, or force<br/>sensor)."]
    box_22{"Are there worn parts?"}
    box_23["Complete the following checks: 1. Check wear on the<br/>vacuum tube. 2. Check wear on the actuator centering<br/>sleeve. 3. Check the assembly robot axes for wear.<br/>4. Check smooth movement of the centering sleeve<br/>relative to the vacuum tube (by disconnecting the<br/>actuator)."]
    box_24["Replace the worn components identified in the<br/>inspection (vacuum tube, centering sleeve, and/or<br/>assembly robot axes)."]
    box_25{"Is the blow off flow (+ duration) correct?"}
    box_26[/"Pneumatic flow measurement procedure"/]
    box_27[/"Refer to the blow off flow and duration check for<br/>variant B machines (medium format parts)."/]
    box_28[/"Refer to the blow off flow and duration check for<br/>variant C machines (large format parts)."/]
    box_29["Resolve clamping issue and replace hose if damaged."]
    box_30{"Is the retracted position of the centering sleeve<br/>relative to the vacuum tube correct?"}
    box_31[/"Refer to the centering sleeve height specification<br/>for variant A machines (small format parts)."/]
    box_32[/"Refer to the centering sleeve height specification<br/>for variant B machines (medium format parts)."/]
    box_33[/"Refer to the centering sleeve height specification<br/>for variant C machines (large format parts)."/]
    box_34["Adjust the retracted position of the centering<br/>sleeve to match the specification, or replace the<br/>centering sleeve assembly if the correct position<br/>cannot be achieved."]
    box_35{"Is the (press down) height of the vacuum tube<br/>relative to 4x part fixture correct?"}
    box_36[/"Refer to the assembly process specification for<br/>variant A machines (small format parts)."/]
    box_37[/"Refer to the assembly process specification for<br/>variant B machines (medium format parts)."/]
    box_38[/"Refer to the assembly process specification for<br/>variant C machines (large format parts)."/]
    box_39["Adjust the press down height of the vacuum tube<br/>relative to the part fixture to match the<br/>specification, or replace the vacuum tube assembly<br/>if the correct height cannot be achieved."]
    box_40{"Is the force sensor working correctly?"}
    box_41[/"Refer to the pre pressure force range specification<br/>for variant A machines (small format parts)."/]
    box_42[/"Refer to the pre pressure force range specification<br/>for variant B machines (medium format parts)."/]
    box_43[/"Refer to the pre pressure force range specification<br/>for variant C machines (large format parts)."/]
    box_44[/"Force sensor calibration procedure for insert<br/>placement"/]
    box_45{"Is the XY placement position of the assembly robot<br/>correct?"}
    box_46[/"Refer to the part alignment specification for<br/>variant A machines (small format parts)."/]
    box_47[/"Refer to the part alignment specification for<br/>variant B machines (medium format parts)."/]
    box_48[/"Refer to the part alignment specification for<br/>variant C machines (large format parts)."/]
    box_49["Set the Z height of the assembly robot to the value<br/>specified in the variant specific assembly process<br/>specification."]
    box_50[/"Assembly robot placement adjustment procedure"/]
    box_51["Perform the assembly robot XY calibration procedure<br/>to correct the insert placement position on the part<br/>fixture."]
    box_52["Verify that the part is lightly pressed into the<br/>insert and is seated without looseness or tilt."]
    box_53(["Placing part on insert is correct"])
    box_54[/"Refer to the vacuum pressure value check for variant<br/>A machines (small format parts), standard vacuum<br/>pressure applies; use the vacuum part present<br/>detection diagnostic only, no variant specific<br/>pressure specification is required for small format<br/>parts."/]
    box_55[/"Refer to the blow off flow and duration check for<br/>variant A machines (small format parts), standard<br/>blow off parameters apply; use the general pneumatic<br/>flow measurement procedure only, no variant specific<br/>blow off calibration is required for small format<br/>parts."/]

